    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s historic downtown still shows red‑brick facades, Italianate and Victorian storefronts that echo its pioneer era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.islands.com/2100222/blissfield-michigan-between-ann-arbor-toledo-laid-back-village-historic-downtown-festivals/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Three bridges once crossed the River Raisin side by side, a unique “Triple Bridges” that served trains and cars until the road bridge was replaced.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blissfield%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During World War II, 16 German POWs working on a nearby sugar beet farm died in a truck‑train collision; they are buried at Fort Custer National Cemetery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blissfield%2C_Michigan"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Blissfield hosts an annual Harvest Festival in October, where flea‑market stalls and craft booths fill the historic downtown streets.",
